diff --git a/docs/libssh2_session_callback_set2.3 b/docs/libssh2_session_callback_set2.3
index ee55af94..1cb39397 100644
--- a/docs/libssh2_session_callback_set2.3
+++ b/docs/libssh2_session_callback_set2.3
@@ -73,6 +73,23 @@ to the abstract pointer set in the \fIlibssh2_session_init_ex(3)\fP call.
 The callback returns the number of bytes read, or \-1 for error. The special
 return code \fB-EAGAIN\fP can be returned to signal that the read was aborted
 to prevent getting blocked and it needs to be called again.
+.IP LIBSSH2_CALLBACK_USERAUTH_BANNER
+Called once for each valid SSH_MSG_USERAUTH_BANNER received before
+authentication succeeds. Banners are still queued and processed normally.
+Multiple, including identical, banners can trigger this callback.
+
+The prototype of the callback:
+
+.nf
+void banner(LIBSSH2_SESSION *session, const char *message,
+            size_t message_length, const char *language,
+            size_t language_length, void **abstract);
+.fi
+
+The message and language pointers are borrowed, are not necessarily
+NUL-terminated, and remain valid only until the callback returns. Copy the
+explicit-length byte ranges before retaining them. The callback runs
+synchronously while the packet is processed and must not block.
 .IP LIBSSH2_CALLBACK_AUTHAGENT
 Called during authentication process to allow the client to connect to the
 ssh-agent and perform any setup, such as configuring the agent or adding keys.
